@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# RQ5 Item-side Diversity Experiments
+
+RQ5 asks whether SIDReasoner concentrates exposure on a few recommended items. We operationalize item-side diversity as exposure concentration in top-10 recommendations:
+
+- Higher `Coverage@10` means broader catalog exposure.
+- Higher `Entropy@10` means exposure is more evenly spread.
+- Lower `Gini@10` means less concentration across the full catalog, including unexposed items.
+
+Assumptions before running:
+
+- Environment, data, and base checkpoints are already present.
+- Root evaluator scripts are available: `evaluate_Qwen3_think.py`, `split.py`, `merge.py`, and the modified `calc.py`.
+- SFT, RA, and released post-RL checkpoints are available under `pretrained/`.
+- The SASRec baseline values used in the paper are encoded in `utils/make_rq5_diversity_tables.py`.
+
+## 0. Optional: Download SFT Checkpoints
+
+The main project setup may already do this. If not:
+
+```bash
+sbatch final_scripts/rq5_diversity/download_sft_checkpoints.sh
+```
+
+This downloads:
+
+- `pretrained/Video_Games/sidreasoner_sft_games`
+- `pretrained/Office_Products/sidreaonser_sft_office`
+
+## 1. Evaluate SFT, RA, and RL Stages
+
+```bash
+sbatch final_scripts/rq5_diversity/evaluate_item_side_diversity.sh
+```
+
+Defaults:
+
+- Datasets: `Video_Games Office_Products`
+- Stages: `sft ra rl`
+- Decoders: `beam10 sample_t12_p095 sample_t10_k50`
+- Seeds: `42 43 44`
+
+All SIDReasoner rows are computed from prediction JSONs, including RL. Existing JSONs can be rescored without regenerating predictions. To evaluate all stages:
+
+```bash
+STAGES="sft ra rl" sbatch final_scripts/rq5_diversity/evaluate_item_side_diversity.sh
+```
+
+Outputs:
+
+- `results/item_side_diversity/manifest_<jobid>.tsv`
+- `results/item_side_diversity/summary_<jobid>.md`
+- per-run JSON files under `results/item_side_diversity/<dataset>/<stage>/`
+
+## 2. Build Paper Tables
+
+After the JSON outputs exist:
+
+```bash
+sbatch final_scripts/rq5_diversity/make_diversity_tables.sh
+```
+
+This writes:
+
+- `results/item_side_diversity/video_games_sft_ra_rl_sasrec_comparison.md`
+- `results/item_side_diversity/office_products_sft_ra_rl_sasrec_comparison.md`
+
+Games values underlie revised Figure 3; Office Products is supplementary.
